The CSS rule to center a div horizontally and vertically can be:

```css
div {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
```

This centers the div both horizontally and vertically within its container. Alternatively, for a more flexible layout using flexbox:

```css
div {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}
```

This approach is often preferred for modern layouts.
